Python: `except A, B:` and `except A, B, C:` (PEP 758, Python 3.14) are now
parsed as a tuple of exception types, like `except (A, B):`, instead of the
Python 2 `except A as B:` form (or a parse error for three or more types).
The Python 2 reading is kept when scanning with `python2` as the language.
